  "id": "pokemon-song-best-collection-cd",
  "name": "Pokémon Song Best Collection CD",
  "category": "product_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "A Japanese CD set released on 1 January 1999 with eleven promo cards, most of them unchanged reprints of the earliest Japanese promos: Arcanine from the Toyota Auto showroom pamphlets of 1997, Cool Porygon and Hungry Snorlax from the Nintendo 64 W Double Get Campaign, Charizard, Blastoise and Venusaur from the 1998 Trade Please campaign, Super Energy Retrieval from the 1997 Pocket Monsters Official Fan Book, and CoroCoro Comic's Computer Error. The one English card was a yellow-cheeked shadowless Base Set Pikachu printed in Japan on Japanese card stock, eight days before Base Set's first English release. It is hard to tell from an ordinary shadowless Pikachu, so a copy in its original seal is the surest proof.",
